HIGH FIX H-4
CONCURRENCY LIMIT ENFORCEMENT
============================================================

Audit finding:

EXECUTION_MAX_CONCURRENT_STEPS is currently metric-only.

Make the configured concurrency limit actually control execution.

Requirements:

- maximum active step executions must never exceed configured limit
- queued steps must wait
- dependency rules must still be respected
- parallel plans must remain parallel up to the limit
- cancellation must clear pending work
- timeout must stop scheduling new work
- failed execution must not deadlock the queue
- retries must respect the same concurrency limit

Do NOT implement a worker queue system.

A lightweight in-process scheduler/semaphore is sufficient.

